        "instructions": "BrowserAI drives a real browser through sessions. A session is a folder holding the browser profile (logins, cookies), downloads, screenshots and a log of every call. Start with browserai_init for a new session or browserai_resume for an existing one; both answer with the session's folder path, which you pass as 'session' to every other tool.\n\nEvery call takes a 'why': write why you are making it, not what it does. It goes in the session's record, and browserai_catch_up reads it back beside what the folder holds now: call it when you arrive at a session you did not create, and before you destroy one.\n\nBrowserAI manages its own browsers. If a browser is missing or broken, call browserai_reinstall_browser.\n\nNothing but browserai_destroy deletes a session: destroy yours when the work is done, and promptly if it held a login."
